{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TauSchurElement","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.TauSchurElement","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TauStructureConstants","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceWeightsOfAlgEquiv","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Nondegenerate"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.abstractSchurElement_indep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.abstractSchurElement_indep","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauSchurElement.lean#L149-L156","doc":"**The independence statement**: the Schur element does not depend on which\ndiagonal matrix unit reads the weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.tau_eq_weightedTrace_inv_abstractSchurElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.tau_eq_weightedTrace_inv_abstractSchurElement","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauSchurElement.lean#L132-L146","doc":"**`τ` is the Schur-weighted character sum** — the identity the Schur\nelements are named for, `τ = Σ_λ (1 / s_λ) χ_λ`.\n\nNo `q ≠ 0` hypothesis: `(c⁻¹)⁻¹ = c` holds in a field unconditionally, so\nthis identity does not depend on the weights being nonzero — only the\n*interpretation* of `s_λ` as a Schur element does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.traceWeight_eq_inv_abstractSchurElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.traceWeight_eq_inv_abstractSchurElement","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauSchurElement.lean#L124-L130","doc":"The weight is the reciprocal of the Schur element — the defining relation,\nin the direction one usually quotes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.abstractSchurElement_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.abstractSchurElement_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauSchurElement.lean#L115-L121","doc":"**The abstract Schur elements never vanish**, at every rank and every\n`q ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.abstractSchurElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.abstractSchurElement","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauSchurElement.lean#L104-L113","doc":"**The abstract Schur element** of the block `i`, relative to a splitting:\nthe reciprocal of `τ`'s weight there.\n\nThis is the *definition* of the Schur element.  Identifying it with Wenzl's\nhook-length product `QOU.MathlibExt.schurElement Q X` is a separate theorem\n(option 3) and is not available here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.traceWeight_tau_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.traceWeight_tau_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauSchurElement.lean#L89-L102","doc":"**Every block weight of `τ` is nonzero**, for any splitting and any\n`q ≠ 0`.\n\nContrapositive of the radical lemma: a zero weight would exhibit a nonzero\nelement annihilated by `τ(· × —)`, and `τ` is nondegenerate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.tau_eq_zero_of_forall_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.tau_eq_zero_of_forall_mul","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauSchurElement.lean#L54-L81","doc":"**`τ` is nondegenerate**: an element killed by `τ(z · —)` is zero.\n\nThe `T_w` coordinates of such a `z` are a left null vector of `tauGram`, and\nthat determinant is nonzero by `tauGram_det_ne_zero`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}